.TH AGENTUSAGE "1" "August 2026" "agentusage v0.10" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agentusage \- persist coding agent transcripts between sessions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agentusage
\fI\,--setup <store-dir>\/\fR
.br
.B agentusage
\fI\,--disable-hook\/\fR
.br
.B agentusage
\fI\,--help\/\fR
.br
.B agentusage
\fI\,--version\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Agentusage is a small utility to set up Claude Code slash commands
(\fI\,/save\/\fP and \fI\,/load\/\fP) and an automatic SessionEnd archiving hook for
persisting session transcripts across projects in a single directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-setup\fR <dir>
set up agentusage with given store directory,
where it will store agent transcripts. Installs
the \fI\,/save\/\fP, \fI\,/load\/\fP, \fI\,/draft\/\fP and \fI\,/cpp\-review\/\fP commands
and registers a SessionEnd hook that auto\-archives
each session to the store via arch\-claude.
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\-hook\fR remove the SessionEnd auto\-archiving hook (leaves
slash commands and permissions in place).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
display this help and exit
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
output version information and exit
